Section 4.3 needs the derivation showing why recall checksum == 0. Present clearly:

设结构体按 32 位字划分为 \( w_0, w_1, \dots, w_{n-1} \)，checksum 字段是最后一个字 \( w_{n-1} \)。保存时先令 \( w_{n-1}=0 \)，计算
\[ s = \mathrm{len} \oplus w_0 \oplus w_1 \oplus \dots \oplus w_{n-2} \oplus 0 \]
并把 \( s \) 写入 checksum 字段。读取时对整块（含 checksum 字段本身）再算一次：
\[ s' = \mathrm{len} \oplus w_0 \oplus \dots \oplus w_{n-2} \oplus s = s \oplus s = 0 \]
由自反律 \( x \oplus x = 0 \)，数据完好时 \( s'=0 \)；任何一字变化都会使 \( s' \neq 0 \)（单字节错必然检出；偶数个对称错误可能对消，XOR 校验的固有局限）。

Wait: "任何一字变化都会使 s'≠0" — a single changed byte always flips the XOR result (since it changes exactly one word by a nonzero delta, XOR of all changes by that delta ≠ 0). Yes: if one word w_i becomes w_i', then s' = old ⊕ (w_i ⊕ w_i') ≠ 0 since w_i ≠ w_i'. Correct. And two errors in different words may cancel if deltas equal. Good.

